WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990
Here are two capacitors.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:04.890
One has twice the
capacitance of the other.

3
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.780
Connect them side by
side across a battery.

4
00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.260
Each gets the same push,
and their charges add up.

5
00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.860
Now join them end to end
instead, one after the other,

6
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.150
in a single loop with the battery.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.580
Which one ends up holding more charge?

8
00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.080
The bigger one, or the smaller one?

9
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll find the combined
capacitance of capacitors side by side

10
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.320
and end to end.

11
00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.310
Then you'll work through a
pair of capacitors in series,

12
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.830
step by step.

13
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.660
Your mission: find out which
capacitor holds more charge,

14
00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:37.880
and explain why.
